  "notes": "キス is a loanword from English \"kiss.\" It is the most common everyday word for a kiss in modern Japanese.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- キス⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to kiss\n- ファーストキス: first kiss\n- キスシーン: kiss scene\n- キス{顔|がお}: kissing face (e.g., in photos)\n\nNATIVE JAPANESE EQUIVALENTS:\n- {接吻|せっぷん}: kiss (formal/literary, often seen in novels)\n- {口|くち}づけ: kiss (poetic/romantic)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nPublic displays of affection including kissing are generally less common in Japan than in Western countries. キス is often talked about in the context of romantic relationships, media, and entertainment rather than casual greetings.",
